, "14.ws-explorer-channel-socket-v2-paxeer-x-feed", "14.ws-explorer-channel-socket-v2-tokens", "14.ws-explorer-join-socket-v2-addresses-address-hash-string", "14.ws-explorer-join-socket-v2-paxeer-x-feed-market-market-id", "14.ws-explorer-join-socket-v2-paxeer-x-feed-new-update", "14.ws-explorer-join-socket-v2-tokens-transaction-hash", "14.ws-explorer-push-addresses-hash-fetched-bytecode", "14.ws-explorer-push-paxeer-x-feed-market-hash-new-update", "14.ws-explorer-push-paxeer-x-feed-new-update-new-update", "14.ws-explorer-push-tokens-hash-total-supply", "4.sol-mocksidiorarouter-revertreason-61b5b636", "6.sol-evmcompatibilitytester-gaslimit-f68016b7", "7.rpc-eth-chainid", "7.rpc-eth-gasprice", "7.rpc-eth-getbalance", "7.rpc-eth-getblockbynumber", "7.rpc-eth-gettransactionreceipt", "8.cfg-ai-evaluator-config-capabilities", "8.cfg-authority-principalpolicy-identities", "8.cfg-authority-registry-assets", "8.cfg-examples-applications", "8.cfg-examples-applications-config", "8.cfg-examples-buyer-agent-application", "8.cfg-examples-marketplace-application", "8.cfg-examples-merchant-checkout-application", "8.cfg-examples-merchant-shop-application", "8.cfg-examples-paid-api-application", "8.cfg-feeder-config-markets", "8.cfg-feeder-config-validator", "8.cfg-ramps-operator-account", "8.cfg-ramps-quotes-context", "8.cfg-release-artifactmanifest-tag", "8.fmt-perf-db-checkpoint", "8.http-gateway-any-explorer"]
interface_review_notes = ["TENDERLY_CHAIN_PATH: transaction_view.ex:588 reads an optional string default /, common-blockscout.env:664 documents the same key, and the template uses it only for the optional Tenderly link; no RPC endpoint is derived from it.", "Frontend config/env rows: configs/app supplies the same feature objects read by the pages, string chain id/name/currency/RPC URLs and API origins; paxeer-x presets select chain 125 and enable Paxeer X. Upstream rollup/beacon/validator panels remain feature/chain gated and are not a claim that a separate LayerX sequencer exists.", "Backend config rows: runtime.exs supplies the named Explorer, web, indexer, logging and Ueberauth keys read by the imported views; optional services retain their feature gates. EmptyBlocksSanitizer batch_size/interval/head_offset and supervisor-disabled settings agree with its readers. The batch result failure is recorded separately.", "HTTP rows: frontend resource templates preserve backend snake_case path parameters and JSON item/pagination envelopes. Upstream chain-specific rollup and MUD pages remain gated to their declared chain/service. Address test fixture drift is address-fixture-shape. The three feed REST contracts agree locally with FeedView but fail across the gateway admission boundary as the three blocking findings describe.", "Feed transport: FeedView.prepare_update emits status ok/error, type 127, accepted per observation, nil recipient and decimal-string prices/fees/gas. Notifier uses that same renderer, filters market topic observations by status 1 and accepted, and the market renderer matches update_hash/index history types. applyPriceUpdates keeps accepted prices ordered by block/index; first-page deduplication, buffer bound and retained-row semantics are reviewed in history findings. Empty join replies have no replay; overview recovery is feed-overview-rejoin.", "Address/token sockets: addresses:<hash> fetched_bytecode shape agrees with the address page; token total_supply is a decimal string at the real producer but numeric in the frontend contract, recorded in token-supply-wire-type. Chain-specific token cache writes are token-chain-cache-key.", "EVM RPC rows: Playwright consumers use standard eth_chainId, eth_gasPrice, eth_getBalance, eth_getBlockByNumber and eth_getTransactionReceipt contracts with hex quantities/hashes. The sanitizer uses the production EthereumJSONRPC batch transport and incorrectly assumes successful non-null results; empty-block-batch-errors records that edge. No member calls node.hyperpaxeer.com as RPC or uses a retired public /rpc path.", "Domain 4 revertReason and domain 6 gasLimit registry crosslinks are lexical matches to EVM JSON fields in RPC views, not calls to MockSidioraRouter or EVMCompatibilityTester getters. Domain 8 config/example/perf-db crosslinks similarly match generic capabilities, identities, assets, applications, config, application, markets, validator, account, context, tag and checkpoint names in UI data/tests; the slice does not load those unrelated producer config files or checkpoint format. The actual domain 8 explorer HTTP transport is reviewed in the gateway findings.", "Archive/signature/status paths: ArchiveView returns frozen:true and verification_status without live status; archive resources use /archive routes; verified transaction signature and committed transaction status views preserve their controller evidence. Account UI omits retired custody/anchor capability rows. BlockView REST and socket paths share native price_update_count. Receipt UI polling and the old test URL are recorded explicitly.", "Security/lifecycle: member UI paths carry read-only producer data; account actions retain upstream session/CSRF and capability feature boundaries. Native signature verification is not bypassed by the views. Route refusals and malformed cursor handling remain explicit. Durable indexing is in backend storage; socket buffers are transient and require reconciliation after connection loss. No source repair or product build/test is asserted by this audit."]
qualification_scope = "Only hf-build (git rev-parse HEAD) and hf-done (declared audit_check.py plus graph checks) qualify this record. Source observations and test contradictions are static review evidence, not claims that application suites ran or that every historical sweep target passed."

